      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ANY QUESTIONS (1) was solid from the back in his WA debut, missing by 2.9L after going back from the wide alley. Out to 1400m is a good sign and now drawing inside can see him closer in the run. NSW form stacks up and he can land the knockout blow. PLACID ROM (2) is a two-start maiden who was unplaced on debut then improved to finish second last time over 1200m at this track, beaten half a length. Has the speed to overcome the draw. Great chance to break through. COSTA STAR (4) finished seventh two runs back then improved last start but found a couple better over 1200m at this track, beaten just 1.5 lengths. Another forward showing is anticipated.RADIO SILENCE (6) is a talented mare who tackled a tougher race at her last run on April 1 and finished eighth behind Wonderfully Made over 2400m in the G3 WA Oaks at Ascot. Blinkers come off; expected to be competitive. WINLOSEWEDRINKBOOZ (3) finds a suitable race today.",
